    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (2 run, 0 failures). Let me summarize the changes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to the v2 spec and made duplicate detection flow entirely through it. All tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n### What changed\n\n**New: `Soundex.java`** \u2014 American Soundex encoding of the last name (first letter + three digits, standard b/f/p/v\u21921 \u2026 r\u21926 mapping with the h/w collapse rule), a package-private helper alongside `ShaHex`/`Household`.\n\n**`ShaHex.java`** \u2014 added `lowerHex(String)` returning the full 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.key(Owner)`** \u2014 now returns `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`. The `householdId` is no longer part of the key. This is also what the API exposes as the `identityKey` field, so the response is now a 64-hex string (satisfies `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`).\n\n**`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 unchanged logic (it already keyed off `OwnerIdentity.key`), so it automatically becomes the *single* 409 check on the new key; the household-derived 409 no longer exists as a separate condition. Still skips soft-deleted owners, still bypassed by `sharesHousehold`, and the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline (400 before this 409). Updated its javadoc and the throw to pass the identity key.\n\n**`CheckOwnerPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 soft-match now triggers when the **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName) and postcode match** (previously: same lastName lowercased + different telephone). Because telephone is now in the key, two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they fall through to this soft match.\n\n**`DuplicateIdentityException`** \u2014 message/constructor now describe the identity key rather than a household id.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 `identityKey` schema description/example updated to the SHA-256 hex form.\n\n### Behavioral effects (per spec)\n- 409 duplicate \u21d4 identical `(normalizedTelephone, lowerEmail, soundex(lastName))`, ignoring deleted owners, blocklist applied first.\n- Same lastName+postcode, different telephone \u2192 **created as a soft match**, not a 409.\n- No separate household-duplicate 409 path remains.",
